    <!-- Accessibility service (Settings > Accessibility > MatChat), shown by the
         system on the enable/consent screen. Called "Background helper" in the
         app (S25, S27). Two jobs: it keeps MatChat connected without the
         "MatChat is running" notification (docs/adr/0008), and it works around
         predictive-text keyboards that consume the right softkey while
         composing. See MatChatKeyAccessibilityService's own doc comment. -->
    <string name="key_accessibility_service_label">MatChat background helper</string>
    <string name="key_accessibility_service_desc">Keeps MatChat connected so new messages arrive
        right away, without the \"MatChat is running\" notification. Also allow MatChat to run in the
        background (MatChat > Settings > Advanced) for this to work.\n\nIt also lets MatChat\'s own right
        softkey (Options or Back, depending on Settings > Advanced > Swap Left/Right keys) work while
        typing a message, on phones whose predictive-text keyboard would otherwise capture it first.
        Reads only the right softkey press — nothing else, never your typing, never the screen.\n\nStill
        not working after turning this on? Only one app\'s accessibility service can win a given key
        press — check Settings > Accessibility for any other keyboard or key-logging service and turn
        it off too. On Android 13 and up, this switch can also silently fail to take effect for a
        sideloaded app like this one until you allow it: open Settings > Apps > MatChat, use the
        overflow menu for \"Allow restricted settings,\" then try turning this on again.</string>
</resources>
